==== REMAINING FOR THE HUMAN (cannot be proven from the Mac) ====
1. pf: bundle host 8081 on the LAN IP is currently: REACHABLE (HTTP 200)
   To block 8081 from the LAN (loopback and the tailnet interface utun4 stay allowed),
   run this once in Terminal (asks for your admin password; lasts until reboot):

   printf 'pass in quick on lo0 proto tcp to any port 8081\npass in quick on utun4 proto tcp to any port 8081\nblock drop in quick proto tcp to any port 8081\n' | sudo pfctl -a com.apple/harness.bundle-host -f - && sudo pfctl -E

   Then re-run this script: the 8081 LAN line should say "not reachable".
2. On the iPhone (on the tailnet), open Expo Go and enter: exp://ryans-mac-studio.tailc3648a.ts.net:8081
   - the app loads (production bundle, no dev menu);
   - in Settings, paste the bearer token (on the Mac: pbcopy < ~/.phone-models/token,
     or read it with: cat ~/.phone-models/token) and save;
   - send a prompt: the reply renders token by token, not all at once;
   - send a long prompt and tap Stop: output halts within a moment and does not resume.
3. On a device on the same Wi-Fi but NOT on the tailnet (or the phone with Tailscale off):
   - https://ryans-mac-studio.tailc3648a.ts.net:8443/v1/state does not resolve/connect;
   - http://192.168.0.27:7789 and :8443 refuse;
   - http://192.168.0.27:8081 refuses once step 1 is done.
